   "statement": "<p>Start with an empty list and carry out a series of commands:</p><ul><li><code>add x</code> — put <code>x</code> at the end;</li><li><code>front x</code> — put <code>x</code> at the very front;</li><li><code>pop</code> — take away the last number (the list is never empty when this happens);</li><li><code>remove x</code> — take away the first <code>x</code> in the list; if there is no <code>x</code>, do nothing;</li><li><code>show</code> — print the list.</li></ul>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>q</code>, the number of commands. Each of the next <code>q</code> lines holds one command.</p>",
   "output": "<p>For every <code>show</code>, one line with the list's numbers separated by single spaces, or <code>empty</code> if the list is empty.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ q ≤ 300; every x is between 1 and 100.</p>",
