   "title": "Best Stretch of k Days",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>A shop records its profit for <code>n</code> days (it can be negative). Find the <code>k</code> consecutive days with the largest total profit. Print that total and the day (counting from 1) the stretch starts. If several stretches tie, give the earliest one.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code> and <code>k</code>. The second line holds the <code>n</code> daily profits.</p>",
   "output": "<p>One line: the largest total and its starting day, separated by a space.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 1000; every profit is between −1000 and 1000.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "7 3\n2 -1 4 3 -2 5 1\n",
     "out": "6 2\n",
     "why": "The stretches total 5, 6, 5, 6 and 4. The first 6 starts on day 2."
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Sliding window: when the window moves one day right, add the day that enters and subtract the day that leaves, instead of adding all <code>k</code> days again.</p>",
   "solution": "n, k = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\ncur = sum(a[:k])\nbest, start = cur, 1\nfor i in range(k, n):\n    cur += a[i] - a[i - k]\n    if cur > best:\n        best, start = cur, i - k + 2\nprint(best, start)",
