   "slug": "counting-off",
   "title": "Counting Off in a Circle",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p><code>n</code> children, numbered 1 to <code>n</code>, stand in a circle. Starting with child 1, they count 1, 2, 3, … around the circle, and the child who says <code>k</code> leaves. The next child starts again from 1, and so on, until everyone has left. Print the order in which the children leave.</p>",
   "input": "<p>One line with <code>n</code> and <code>k</code>.</p>",
   "output": "<p>The numbers of the children in the order they leave, separated by single spaces.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 200; 1 ≤ k ≤ 1000.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "7 3\n",
     "out": "3 6 2 7 5 1 4\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Keep the children still in the circle in a list, and the index of the child who will say \"1\". The child who says <code>k</code> is <code>k − 1</code> places further on, wrapping around with <code>%</code>. After <code>pop</code>, the next child slides into that same index.</p>",
   "solution": "n, k = map(int, input().split())\ncircle = list(range(1, n + 1))\ni = 0\nout = []\nwhile circle:\n    i = (i + k - 1) % len(circle)\n    out.append(circle.pop(i))\nprint(*out)",
   "explanation": "",
